From 2a3f9dedfc395e644a8c9fab7911628e8fb56f4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:21:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 34/65] Represent the turn block +$192 as CokTurn and port more
 H027 handlers

The +$192 block keeps its $18 bytes; its only longword, the target
character at +$C, becomes a C pointer.  H005+$2A14, $2B32 (combatants)
and $16 (fallen characters) become C globals.  New: H062+$02FA, $2650,
H063+$2B7C, H027+$0214, $0338, $2182 and the handlers for effects $16,
$17, $1A, $2B, $2C, $30, $31, $3A, $3D, $3E, $40-$42, $44, $45, $51,
$56-$58, $72, $73, $75.  H048+$16D4 keeps only its non-combat return.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013G8KST8dgGfenpqx3RukYi
